here we need to be  so convenient and too tempting for some  to pass up i said  it must be meant to be let me go get a  shot  u.s airlines which lost 35 billion  dollars in 2020  are celebrating their return to travel  1.5 million passengers are expected to  pass through atlanta  the nation's busiest airport this  weekend the biggest crowd since december  2019.  restaurant owners are also predicting  big business it's going to be crazy  people have been  dying to get out most states have lifted  mask and social distancing requirements  just in time for the holiday weekend  desperate to welcome in patrons and  tourists  and their money jennifer johnson global  news  washington still ahead the new covet  surge in the uk  and the warnings for canada  you're watching global national  [Music]  it was a terrifying scene just minutes  into a ferry trip in indonesia  close to 200 people were on board when  the ferry caught fire  all the passengers and crew were forced  to jump ship  fortunately fishing boats in the area  helped take the survivors to a nearby  remote island all 181 passengers and 14  crew members are  safe but it's still not clear what  started the fire  vietnam says it has detected a new coven  19 variant that's a hybrid of strains  first found in india and britain  scientists discovered it while examining  the genetic makeup of the virus that  recently infected some patients  lab tests suggest this hybrid may spread  more easily by  air than other variants and that it  could be responsible for vietnam's surge  in cases the country initially had  success battling the virus  but in recent weeks it has recorded more  than 3 500  new cases the variant first detected in  india is rapidly spreading across  britain it  is now the dominant strain in the uk the  country has reported its highest level  of infections in almost two months  and as redmond shannon explains there's  concern the variant could delay the  country's  final stage of reopening  [Music]  england is nearly there in three weeks  the last restrictions are set to be  lifted  but the british government says a slow  rise in covet 19 cases again  threatens that goal it's partly down to  the b1  617.2 or india variant  which is believed to be more  transmissible although not necessarily  more deadly the latest estimates are  that more than half  and potentially as many as three  quarters  of all new cases are now of this variant  the new dominance of the variant coming  just after indoor dining and  drinking resumed makes it difficult to  know  what is driving the rise but i want to  stress that  we always did expect to see an increase  in cases that was always going to happen  variant cases are clustered in a few  cities and the highest coveted infection  rates are among  unvaccinated young people last week  there was a week when  one percent of bolton's 10 to 14 year  olds tested positive  i mean that's incredibly high we know  from public health england that attack  rate so the chance of you being affected  if you're a contact from someone with  the indian variant is over 50 higher  than  if it was a contact with the old kent  variant research suggests  a second vaccine dose is crucial against  this variant according to official  figures it currently makes up just a  tiny fraction of cases in canada  i wouldn't be surprised in the months to  come that we definitely start to see a  rise in the b161  7.2 variant if that happens provinces  will be  racing to get not just one but two doses  into canadian arms  but only focusing on canadians will be  short-sighted  according to global public health expert  ananya banerjee  we are on divergence of a vaccine  apartheid  and that we need to make sure at least  10 percent of each country  globally are vaccinated particularly  seniors and healthcare workers  she says unless richer nations ensure  that happens  other variants will appear one of which  might even evade vaccines and  put us all back to square one redmond  